# Machine owner file for the "ccache" and "sccache" rows in TOOLCHAIN.md.
# Format: `key=value`, `#` comments. Consumed by tools/bootstrap and tools/doctor.
#
# The two are registered separately in tools/lib/pins.sh because they are
# separate tools with separate evidence: ccache has a measured result and
# sccache has none. A single row read only its first key, so the second version
# reached TOOLCHAIN.md with no gate behind it.
#
# ccache is the clang warm-rebuild layer (`cc_wrapper` in the dev GN args
# profiles); sccache is the Rust RUSTC_WRAPPER, local disk only. Decision 0013
# also specified a shared object-store backend for a hosted CI runner; decision
# 0023 abolished the runner and decision 0200 rules out this project operating
# the store, so that half is retired rather than pending. Siso's own local
# cache is part of Chromium and is not pinned here.
#
# Pinned at SP-01 (2026-08-17, Chromium milestone 152) to the versions that
# produced the first recorded build. Both are host tooling, so these are the
# versions a builder must have, not versions the Chromium build selects.
#
# The ccache-under-Siso question this file was waiting on is answered, and the
# answer is uncomfortable: ccache runs, but 90.06% of the build's 44,338
# compiler invocations were uncacheable, every one reported as "Could not use
# modules" — Chromium 152 compiles Android targets with C++ modules that ccache
# 4.9.1 will not handle. Siso was not the obstacle. Only 9.94% of calls were
# cacheable and a cold cache cannot hit any of them, so the warm-rebuild value
# of that remainder is still unmeasured. Whether `cc_wrapper = "ccache"` stays
# in the dev profiles is OD-075 (decide by M1), with the measurement written up
# in docs/development/chromium-fork-and-build.md section 6 item 2.
#
# sccache is unexercised: it is the Rust RUSTC_WRAPPER and no Rust target has
# been built under GN yet. The version below is what is installed, not a
# measured result.

ccache=4.9.1
sccache=0.17.0

# Local cache sizes applied by tools/bootstrap. Sized for the Chromium host
# hardware guidance in decision 0013 (>= 400 GB free on a 1 TB NVMe).
ccache_max_size=100G
sccache_cache_size=50G
